{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1860","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1860","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1860\",\"parent_revision\":\"1179e2c9b7fc8068195a7c56f5e7010475c3e2a0acafc5820091ccaa75fd3c90\",\"root_revision\":\"1179e2c9b7fc8068195a7c56f5e7010475c3e2a0acafc5820091ccaa75fd3c90\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-04-27\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add dirty-repo stash prompt before worktree creation in work-milestone** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md \u2014 pattern: Dirty Repo Stashing (feature 10)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-21)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\n| Input | Classification | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | PRESENT | Item description + research/insights/2026-04-20-orchestra-improvements.md \u00a76 |\\n| Scope boundaries | PRESENT | Confined to `work-milestone` Step 3 + new shell script + ephemeral JSON state file |\\n| External interfaces | PRESENT | `git status --porcelain`, `git stash push/list`, `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/auto-stashes.json` |\\n| Constraints | DERIVABLE | Interactive prompt required; N is default; must run on main before worktrees are created |\\n| Existing system context | PRESENT | Confirmed zero stash handling in `plugins/development-harness/**` via grep |\\n| Verification expectations | PRESENT | Measurable signals defined: prompt string, stash list match, JSON file, reminder string |\\n\\nNo MISSING conditions. No blockers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. In any git repo with uncommitted changes, run `echo x > scratch.txt` (creates a dirty state).\\n2. Invoke `/dh:work-milestone 1` (or any valid milestone number with a dispatch plan).\\n3. Observe whether a prompt containing `\\\"Stash uncommitted changes\\\"` appears before worktree creation.\\n\\n**Current (broken) behavior**: The skill lists \\\"Clean git state on main\\\" as an entry condition at `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` line 18 but provides no action. The user either receives an implicit failure or must hand-stash and re-invoke.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Running `grep -r \\\"git stash\\\\|stash push\\\\|uncommitted\\\" plugins/development-harness/` returns zero matches \u2014 confirms no stash handling exists today.\\n- `work-milestone/SKILL.md` line 18: `\\\"Clean git state on main\\\"` listed as entry condition without a recovery path.\\n- Source pattern confirmed: `research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md` lines 144\u2013150 describe Orchestra's Step 2c: prompt user \u2192 `git stash push -m \\\"orchestra-auto-stash: pre-run {branch_name}\\\"` \u2192 record stash ref for post-run reminder.\\n- Prior analysis at `research/insights/2026-04-20-orchestra-improvements.md` \u00a76 (\\\"Improvement 6\\\") classifies this as high-confidence, medium-impact, and records `#1860` as the tracking item.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 The entry condition \\\"Clean git state on main\\\" is listed but unenforceable without recovery. A user who does not notice it may silently lose work when worktree mechanics interact with their dirty working tree. The fix is low-complexity and has a well-defined source pattern (Orchestra). Deferral carries active risk of user data loss.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Users with any uncommitted work who want to invoke `/dh:work-milestone` \u2014 they must manually stash and re-invoke.\\n- Bottleneck: Entry gate at `work-milestone/SKILL.md` line 18 with no resolution path creates a silent failure or hard stop.\\n- Risk: A user who proceeds without noticing the condition check may encounter undefined worktree behaviour against a dirty main working tree.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Users can invoke `/dh:work-milestone` from any working state without ceremony.\\n- Auto-stash records are durable (`auto-stashes.json`) so the restore reminder survives across sessions.\\n- The script (`prepare_clean_worktree.sh`) is reusable by any future skill that needs the same pre-worktree clean-state guarantee (e.g., `--worktree` flag for `work-backlog-item`, issue #974).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `/dh:work-milestone` is invoked with uncommitted changes present on main, the skill:\\n\\n1. Detects the dirty state using `git status --porcelain` before any worktree is created.\\n2. Presents a user prompt: `Stash uncommitted changes? [y/N]`.\\n3. On `y`: runs `git stash push -m \\\"dh-auto-stash: pre-run {branch}\\\"`, records the stash ref in `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/auto-stashes.json` keyed by branch name, then continues to Step 3 (integration branch creation and worktree add).\\n4. On `N` or no answer: halts with a clear message directing the user to commit or stash manually before re-invoking.\\n5. On skill completion: prints a reminder containing `git stash pop {ref}` so the user knows how to restore their work.\\n\\nWhen invoked with a clean working tree, the pre-check exits silently with no user interaction.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- A new script `plugins/development-harness/scripts/prepare_clean_worktree.sh` (or Python equivalent following the repository's language conventions) that:\\n  - Runs `git status --porcelain`; exits 0 immediately if clean\\n  - Prompts `Stash uncommitted changes? [y/N]` if dirty\\n  - On `y`: stashes with label `dh-auto-stash: pre-run {branch}`, writes ref to `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/auto-stashes.json`\\n  - On `N`: exits non-zero so the caller can halt\\n- `work-milestone/SKILL.md` Step 3 updated to call this script before `git worktree add`, with the entry condition at line 18 updated to describe the recovery path.\\n- On completion (Step 10), `work-milestone` reads `auto-stashes.json` and prints any pending stash restore reminder.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. With a dirty main working tree, invoking `/dh:work-milestone` (or the prepare script directly) prints a prompt containing the literal string `\\\"Stash uncommitted changes\\\"` before any `git worktree add` executes.\\n2. Answering `y` at the prompt results in `git stash list` showing an entry matching `dh-auto-stash:` with the integration branch name.\\n3. After `y`, `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/auto-stashes.json` exists and contains the key `branch` matching the integration branch name and the stash ref.\\n4. Answering `N` (or pressing Enter) halts the skill with a non-zero exit and a message directing the user to stash or commit manually before re-invoking.\\n5. With a clean working tree, invoking `/dh:work-milestone` proceeds to Step 3 without any stash prompt appearing.\\n6. On milestone completion, stdout contains the string `git stash pop` alongside the recorded stash ref.\\n7. The prepare script (or equivalent) is callable independently of `work-milestone` so it can be reused by future skills (e.g., `--worktree` flag for `work-backlog-item`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Source pattern | `research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md` lines 144\u2013150 (Orchestra Step 2c: Dirty Repo Stashing) |\\n| Prior analysis | `research/insights/2026-04-20-orchestra-improvements.md` \u00a76 (Improvement 6) |\\n| Primary file | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` (lines 18, 34\u201337, Step 3) |\\n| Entry condition | Line 18: \\\"Clean git state on main\\\" \u2014 the insertion point for the recovery path |\\n| Kage-bunshin spawn script | `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py` (worktree creation flow reference) |\\n| DH state path convention | `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/` \u2014 existing ephemeral context directory |\\n| Git stash reference | `.claude/skills/modern-git/references/git-workflows.md` lines 228\u2013231 |\\n| Sibling feature | Backlog #974 \u2014 `--worktree` flag for `work-backlog-item` (future consumer of the reusable script) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 the codebase gap is confirmed, the insertion point is known, and the source pattern is documented. No upstream blockers.\\n- Blocks: Backlog #974 (`--worktree` flag for `work-backlog-item`) could reuse the new prepare script once it exists.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the change is a new script (< 60 lines) + a SKILL.md update at one insertion point (Step 3) + one completion-step reminder. The logic is a direct port of Orchestra's Step 2c with a DH-specific stash label and state file path. No new MCP tools, no schema changes, no dependencies to resolve.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` (line 18) lists \\\"Clean git state on main\\\" as an entry condition but provides no action to achieve clean state \u2014 if the user is dirty, the skill fails the condition with no recovery path.\\n\\nGrep of `plugins/development-harness/**` for `git stash`, `stash push`, or `uncommitted` returns no matches. `implement-feature` does not check for dirty state at all before its sibling skills create worktrees.\\n\\nSymptom: a user with uncommitted work is forced to hand-stash and re-invoke. Worse, a user who does not notice the condition check may proceed and silently lose work when worktree mechanics interact with their dirty state.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` (line 18) lists \\\"Clean git state on main\\\" as an entry condition but provides no action to achieve clean state \u2014 if the user is dirty, the skill fails the condition with no recovery path.\\n\\nGrep of `plugins/development-harness/**` for `git stash`, `stash push`, or `uncommitted` returns no matches. `implement-feature` does not check for dirty state at all before its sibling skills create worktrees.\\n\\nSymptom: a user with uncommitted work is forced to hand-stash and re-invoke. Worse, a user who does not notice the condition check may proceed and silently lose work when worktree mechanics interact with their dirty state.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA reusable `plugins/development-harness/scripts/prepare_clean_worktree.sh` is added. It runs `git status --porcelain`, and if non-empty, prompts the user: \\\"Stash uncommitted changes? [y/N]\\\". On `y` it runs `git stash push -m \\\"dh-auto-stash: pre-run {branch}\\\"` and records the stash ref in `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/auto-stashes.json`. `work-milestone` Step 3 calls this script before `git worktree add`. On completion, the skill prints a reminder: `Auto-stash ref X pending; run 'git stash pop {ref}' to restore.`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- In a repo with `echo x > scratch.txt`, invoking `/dh:work-milestone 1` prints a y/N prompt with the literal string `\\\"Stash uncommitted changes\\\"`.\\n- On `y`, `git stash list` shows an entry matching `dh-auto-stash:`, and `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/auto-stashes.json` exists with key `branch` matching the integration branch name.\\n- On skill completion, stdout contains the reminder string `git stash pop`.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2dc8157230593ade49e77af8911e0811f30a374386a1d37535e587b40462f151\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCvCxQ\"}"}